Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Enable Objective-C before the compile flags are mirrored

The compiler flag macros write CMAKE_OBJCXX_FLAGS as they run, and
OptionsCommon runs them before Options${PORT} enables OBJC and OBJCXX. The
variable then exists before CMake initializes it from the toolchain and the
environment, so those flags never reach the Objective-C++ compile rules:
the WTF precompiled header was built without -DWEBKIT_IOS6=1, the -include
prefix headers, -nostdinc++ and the target, so ENABLE(COCOA_WEBM_PLAYER)
was on and the build stopped on its MEDIA_SOURCE check. C++ sources already
had the full set.

Enable the two languages before the first flag macro runs.
---
diff --git a/Source/cmake/WebKitCommon.cmake b/Source/cmake/WebKitCommon.cmake
--- a/Source/cmake/WebKitCommon.cmake
+++ b/Source/cmake/WebKitCommon.cmake
@@ -335,6 +335,7 @@
         include(WebKitAdditions)
     endif ()
 
+    enable_language(OBJC OBJCXX)
     include(OptionsCommon)
     include(Options${PORT})
 
